Third-party code and dependencies of this branch
================================================

The JM2D code in this repository (jm2d_maze/, safediffusion/ except safediffusion/armtdpy/, configs/, paper/,
scripts/, tests/) is released under the MIT License in LICENSE. The following parts come from, or are derived
from, other projects and keep their own terms.

robomimic/  (vendored, trimmed and modified)
  robomimic, https://github.com/ARISE-Initiative/robomimic, MIT License,
  Copyright (c) 2021 Stanford Vision and Learning Lab. The original license text is in robomimic/LICENSE.
  Modifications for this project: the diffusion-policy algorithm (robomimic/algo/diffusion_policy.py, whose
  conditional 1-D UNet follows Diffusion Policy, Chi et al., https://github.com/real-stanford/diffusion_policy, MIT
  License), the safediffusion config registration, and the removal of unused algorithms, environments and scripts.

safediffusion/armtdpy/reachability/conSet/  (vendored, unmodified)
  Zonotope and polynomial-zonotope set representations from the Python implementation of ARMTD
  (Autonomous Reachability-based Manipulator Trajectory Design; Holmes, Kousik et al.), authored by Yongseok Kwon,
  ROAHM Lab, University of Michigan (file headers credit the author).
  OPEN ITEM before public release: confirm the license of this code with its authors / ROAHM Lab.

zonopy  (optional dependency, not redistributed)
  https://github.com/roahmlab/zonopy. Only used when USE_ZONOPY=true; the default is the vendored conSet above.

d4rl  (dependency, not redistributed)
  The padded mazes require the fork goldenhazard/D4RL@a0b30c4e27c24a4ec9600b211a1b549b13c867b6 of D4RL
  (https://github.com/Farama-Foundation/D4RL, Apache License 2.0), installed from requirements.txt.

diffusers  (dependency, not redistributed)
  https://github.com/huggingface/diffusers, Apache License 2.0. JM2DPolicy.get_noise
  (safediffusion/algo/jm2d_policy.py) inverts the forward-noising formula of diffusers' DDPMScheduler.add_noise.

jm2d_maze/reachability/  (this work)
  Forward-reachable-set tensor of the HQ backup planner and the MATLAB scripts that generate it with the CORA
  toolbox (https://tumcps.github.io/CORA/, not redistributed).

Other dependencies (PyTorch, MuJoCo / mujoco-py, gym, cyipopt / IPOPT, NumPy, SciPy, ...) are installed separately
and are not redistributed here.
